      "content": "Your feelings of failure are incredibly painful, but remember that wanting to protect your child from harm shows how much you care, not that you are hurting them. Many parents believe their presence causes struggle; the real weight comes from perfectionism and the pressure to fix everything so the child can be effortless. You are not defined by this moment, and perhaps the most powerful thing you can give your child is a life where they are free from your fear rather than a shield. Please consider reaching out to a therapist who specializes in parental anxiety, as a professional can help you move through these depths with someone who truly listens.",
